<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">2 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 2 December, from 1697 to 1971.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1697 CE <span class="tih-ago">329 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wren's new St Paul's Cathedral holds its first service</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The choir of Christopher Wren's new St Paul's opened for worship with a thanksgiving service for the Peace of Ryswick. The cathedral, replacing the one lost in the Great Fire, was declared complete in 1711.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1804 CE <span class="tih-ago">222 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon crowns himself emperor at Notre-Dame</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the presence of Pope Pius VII, Napoleon placed the imperial crown on his own head and then crowned Josephine. The ceremony proclaimed a new hereditary monarchy born of the Revolution.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1805 CE <span class="tih-ago">221 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon defeats Austria and Russia at Austerlitz</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the first anniversary of his coronation, Napoleon routed a larger Austro-Russian army at Austerlitz in Moravia. The 'Battle of the Three Emperors' knocked Austria out of the Third Coalition.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1942 CE <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fermi's team achieves the first controlled nuclear chain reaction</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Under the stands of Stagg Field at the University of Chicago, Enrico Fermi's team started a self-sustaining chain reaction in Chicago Pile-1. It opened the way to atomic bombs and nuclear power.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1971 CE <span class="tih-ago">55 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The United Arab Emirates is founded</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Six of the Trucial States, led by Abu Dhabi and Dubai, formed the United Arab Emirates after Britain's withdrawal from the Gulf. Ras al-Khaimah joined in 1972.</p></div></li></ol>
